ns.WhatsNew = {
    { version = "7.1.4", text = "Your bags can now mark the gear in your equipment sets, and the Loot Feed shows how many of each item you already have. Auras above and below the unit frames go back to the corner.\n\n|cffffffffWe need your help testing:|r\n• |cffffffffBags, Equipment Set Icon:|r turn it on in |cffffffffItem Icons|r. Items in any of your equipment sets should show a small padlock in the top left corner, and nothing else should.\n• |cffffffffLoot Feed, Owned Count:|r loot an item you already carry. Its icon should show your new total.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things change even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffUnit frames, auras Above the Frame and Below the Frame:|r back in the corner, as before 7.1.3.\n• |cffffffffLoot Feed:|r item icons now show how many you have in your bags. Turn it off under |cffffffffShow|r.\n• |cffffffffBags & Looting, Item Slots:|r six switches became one |cffffffffItem Icons|r dropdown, and |cffffffffPlain Empty Slots|r moved into |cffffffffSkin Item Slots|r. What you picked is kept.\n• |cffffffffNew players only:|r |cffffffffChat Style|r starts on |cffffffffClassic Style|r. Your setup stays as it is.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Bags & Looting|r\n• |cffffffffEquipment Set Icon|r (off): a small padlock on bag items in one of your equipment sets. It's only a marker: you can still sell the item.\n• |cffffffffLoot Feed, Owned Count|r (on): how many you have in your bags, on each item's icon.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• |cffffffffBags & Looting, Item Icons:|r one dropdown in place of |cffffffffJunk Coin|r, |cffffffffItem Level|r, |cffffffffUncollected Appearances|r, |cffffffffPet Food Marker|r and |cffffffffBoE Text|r, with the new |cffffffffEquipment Set Icon|r.\n• |cffffffffBags & Looting, Skin Item Slots:|r |cffffffffPlain Empty Slots|r is now a choice here. It works with the skin |cffffffffOff|r too.\n• |cffffffffLoot Feed, Show:|r one dropdown in place of |cffffffffShow Money|r and |cffffffffShow Skill-Ups|r, with the new |cffffffffOwned Count|r.\n• |cffffffffChat Style:|r |cffffffffReset|r goes to |cffffffffClassic Style|r.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• |cffffffffProc glows:|r Stormstrike and other spells with their own cooldown glowed as if their cooldown had reset.\n• |cffffffffNameplates, hunters below level 12:|r plates out of range didn't fade.\n\n|cffe6cc99Translations|r\n• French updated for 7.1.3. By Brainc3ll.\n• Simplified and Traditional Chinese updated for 7.1.3. By AreChen." },
    { version = "7.1.3", text = "Raid frames you can set up per raid size, nameplates that show the whole plate when the unit itself starts a fight, and borders on the meter's bars. New players now start with a ready-made setup, and yours stays as it is.\n\n|cffffffffWe need your help testing:|r\n• |cffffffffRaid frames:|r in Edit Mode, pick a |cffffffffRaid Size|r and change something. Join a raid of that size and check your change is there, and only there.\n• |cffffffffNameplates, Show Whole Plate > When It Fights:|r a Name Only plate should show in full while that unit is fighting, even when you aren't.\n• |cffffffffMeters:|r each bar has a FlareUI Thin border. Try every bar style, with class icons on and off.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things change even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffNew players only:|r FlareUI's defaults changed for new installs. Your setup stays exactly as it is, with one exception:\n      - |cffffffffFlareUI Style, frames you never moved:|r focus, pet, target of target, target of focus, totems and flag carriers sit up to 20 pixels from where they were. Move them back in Edit Mode if you like.\n• |cffffffffNameplates, Show Plates in Combat:|r moved. It's now |cffffffffName Only Mode > Show Whole Plate > When You Fight|r, set for each plate type. What you picked before is kept.\n• |cffffffffDelete Junk When Full:|r moved from Quality of Life to |cffffffffBags & Looting > Bags > Tweaks|r. Your setting is kept.\n• |cffffffffMeters:|r each bar now has a FlareUI Thin border in place of Blizzard's bright edge.\n• |cffffffffTotem bar:|r its timers read like the unit frames': bare seconds, then \"m\" and \"h\".\n• |cffffffffGryphons on Always:|r they now dim with the main action bar when something dims it, like OLEDGuard.\n• |cffffffffParty and raid frames, Tooltips module off:|r aura icons now show their tooltips, as on Blizzard's frames.\n\n|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffRaid frames, every setting per Raid Size:|r up to 10, 25 and 40 players each keep their own Edit Mode settings. A size you never change uses your shared settings.\n• |cffffffffNameplates, Show Whole Plate:|r in Name Only Mode, show the whole plate |cffffffffWhen You Fight|r, |cffffffffWhen It Fights|r, or both.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• |cffffffffShow Whole Plate|r (None): in the Name Only Mode section, for each plate type. |cffffffffWhen It Fights|r shows the whole plate while that unit is in a fight.\n• |cffffffffCrowd Control, Aura Icon Shape, Aura Swipe and Aura Timer:|r back, for the Crowd Control and Defensives icons. Until you pick one, each follows the Auras section.\n• |cffffffffTest in Game:|r plates also show sample buffs, debuffs, crowd control and defensives, and the elite and rare dragons.\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• |cffffffffRaid frames:|r every Edit Mode setting is saved per |cffffffffRaid Size|r, except positions, main tank frames, icons and Fading.\n\n|cffe6cc99Meters|r\n• |cffffffffBar borders:|r each bar in a FlareUI Thin border over a dark fill.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• |cffffffffUnit frames, auras Above the Frame and Below the Frame:|r centred on the frame.\n• |cffffffffAuras on two rows:|r the icons line up in columns on every frame. Before, the ones after purgeable buffs or weapon enchants sat 2 pixels over.\n• |cffffffffChat, Modern edit box:|r shorter, to fit one line of text.\n• |cffffffffEdit Mode:|r\n      - A dropdown with several picks reads |cffffffffNone|r when nothing is ticked.\n      - The Fading box under Blizzard's frames, like the chat, puts its switches two to a line.\n      - |cffffffffCentred Spell Name|r is the last choice in the cast bar's |cffffffffShow|r list.\n      - |cffffffffPvP Flag|r and |cffffffffPvP Timer|r are the last choices in the unit frames' |cffffffffIcons|r list.\n• |cffffffffNameplates, Crowd Control and Defensives:|r a little further from the plate.\n• |cffffffffMinimap, Info Bar:|r |cffffffffBelow the Map|r is now a |cffffffffPosition|r dropdown (On the Map, Below the Map).\n• |cffffffffMinimap, Addon Buttons:|r |cffffffffOpen on Mouseover|r is now |cffffffffOpen Drawer on Mouseover|r, and |cffffffffOnly on Mouseover|r is |cffffffffAddon Buttons Only on Mouseover|r.\n• |cffffffffMeters, Threat Window:|r |cffffffffOff|r is now |cffffffffMeters Tab|r, and |cffffffffIn the Meter in Combat|r is |cffffffffAuto-Switch in Combat|r.\n• |cffffffffSettings:|r many pages reordered so related options sit together, among them Action Bars, XP Bar, Minimap, Quest Tracker, Tooltips, Quality of Life, Meters and Nameplates' Cast Bars.\n• |cffffffffTooltips:|r |cffffffffShow PvP|r shows its line in the preview. |cffffffffHealing and Damage|r takes a full row.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• |cffffffffPet frame, Range Check:|r stayed faded with your pet right next to you when you weren't in a group.\n• |cffffffffChat:|r a new size in |cffffffffSettings > Chat > Fonts|r didn't reach a window whose size you had picked from its tab.\n• |cffffffffMeters, Bar Texture:|r going back to |cffffffffBlizzard|r kept the texture you had picked.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r Blizzard's sample auras showed on real plates in Edit Mode.\n\n|cffe6cc99Translations|r\n• French updated for 7.1.2. By Brainc3ll." },
    { version = "7.1.2", text = "One cast bar for a whole batch of crafts, aura timers that read like Blizzard's, and a safer way to reset your settings. Plus fixes for the bugs 7.1.1 brought to the Cooldown Manager and the chat.\n\n|cffffffffWe need your help testing:|r\n• |cffffffffCrafting:|r turn on |cffffffffShow Craft Batch|r and make 5 of something. One cast bar should run over the whole batch, with the count beside the timer.\n• |cffffffffNameplate timers:|r an aura longer than a minute should show no timer on a nameplate. Under 10 seconds, the timer turns yellow, then red.\n• |cffffffffShamans:|r with Improved Stormstrike, Stormstrike should glow on your bars when it resets.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things change even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffAura timers|r now read like Blizzard's:\n      - The buff and debuff icons by the minimap keep \"s\", \"m\" and \"h\".\n      - Unit frames show seconds as a bare number, with \"m\" and \"h\" above a minute.\n      - Nameplates show seconds as a bare number, and no timer on an aura longer than a minute.\n• |cffffffffQuality of Life, Craft Batch Time:|r removed. |cffffffffShow Craft Batch|r on the Player Cast Bar replaces it, and starts off.\n• |cffffffffChat:|r every chat window follows |cffffffffSettings > Chat > Fonts|r again. A font size you picked for a single window on 7.1.1 is cleared once. Pick it again from the tab's right-click menu.\n• |cffffffffCooldown Manager, Growth From the Middle:|r the icons centre on the box where you placed the bar in Edit Mode. This replaces 7.1.1's change, which could push them off the box.\n• |cffffffffNameplates, Show Enemy Plates / Show Friendly Plates:|r if one is set to |cffffffffIn Combat|r and you turn plates on in Blizzard's settings outside a fight, FlareUI now takes that as your choice and switches to |cffffffffAlways|r.\n\n|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffShow Craft Batch:|r crafting several of one item runs one Player Cast Bar over the whole batch. The timer shows the time left for all of them, then how many are made, like (2/5).\n• |cffffffffReset Profile:|r resets only the profile in use, so a setup that went wrong no longer means losing every character's settings.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• |cffffffffPlayer Cast Bar, Show Craft Batch|r (off): in Edit Mode, under the cast bar's |cffffffffShow|r list as |cffffffffCraft Batch|r. Works on the Player Cast Bar and on the player frame's cast bar.\n• |cffffffffSettings, Fonts, Player Cast Bar:|r shows the cast bar itself, casting, while you change its fonts.\n\n|cffe6cc99Action Bars|r\n• |cffffffffProc Glow:|r lights Stormstrike when Improved Stormstrike resets it. The glow goes out when you use it, or after 8 seconds. Works on macros that cast it.\n\n|cffe6cc99Chat|r\n• |cffffffffFont Size|r in the chat tab's right-click menu. A size picked there is that window's own.\n\n|cffe6cc99Profiles|r\n• |cffffffffReset Profile:|r puts the profile in use back to FlareUI's defaults. Your other profiles stay as they are.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• |cffffffffReset FlareUI:|r its warning now says it resets every profile on all your characters.\n• |cffffffffNameplates, Click-Through:|r the description now says it's one setting for every plate type.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• |cffffffffRaid frames, Raid Size:|r picking a size now updates Width, Height and Power Height in the Edit Mode dialog. Your values were always saved per size.\n• |cffffffffCooldown Manager:|r Tracked Buffs with 6 or more auras sat off-centre.\n• |cffffffffCooldown Manager:|r Essential and Utility icons could sit far to one side of their box.\n• |cffffffffChat:|r new and whisper windows stopped following your Fonts size.\n• |cffffffffNameplates:|r plates turned on in Blizzard's settings were turned off again at every login while In Combat was picked.\n• |cffffffffLoot Window:|r Blizzard's empty Loot Window box showed beside FlareUI's in Edit Mode.\n• |cffffffffSettings:|r opening General with |cffffffffSync Blizzard UI|r off could cause an error. By AreChen.\n• |cffffffffBags and Loot Window:|r the German and Korean \"BoE\" marks were too long to fit on the icon.\n\n|cffe6cc99Translations|r\n• French updated for 7.1.1. By Brainc3ll.\n• Hungarian updated for 7.1.1. By Xentinus." },
    { version = "7.1.1", text = "Your requests, built: raid frames that size themselves to the raid, a Battleground choice in every Visibility list, and fading for party, raid and boss frames. Plus a pile of fixes from Discord.\n\n|cffffffffRestart the game fully after updating.|r This version adds new files, and a /reload doesn't load them.\n\n|cffffffffWe need your help testing:|r\n• |cffffffffRaid frames:|r pick a |cffffffffRaid Size|r in Edit Mode, change its Width, then join raids of different sizes. The frames should switch size.\n• |cffffffffSync Blizzard UI:|r log in on an alt. It should ask you once whether to copy, and never again.\n• |cffffffffGryphons:|r with Action Bar 1's Icon Size below 100%, drag them and nudge them with the arrow keys. They should move smoothly.\n• |cffffffffFake Cooldown Manager:|r turn on |cffffffffShow Only When Ready|r and use a spell with a long cooldown.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things change even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffVisibility, In an Instance:|r now means dungeons and raids only. Battlegrounds and arenas have their own choice, |cffffffffIn a Battleground|r. Every list that had In an Instance ticked gets In a Battleground ticked too, so nothing hides or shows differently.\n• |cffffffffSync Blizzard UI:|r no longer copies on its own.\n      - Each of your other characters asks once, at its next login. After that, copy with |cffffffffCopy Now|r.\n      - Characters that already synced aren't asked. They get one chat line instead.\n      - |cffffffffHide Pop-up Alerts|r is gone.\n• |cffffffffQuality of Life, Nameplate Combo Points:|r back, and off by default. 7.1 always showed combo points on Blizzard's nameplates. Turn it on to keep them.\n• |cffffffffGryphons:|r if Action Bar 1's Icon Size is below 100% and you moved your gryphons, they shift once. Place them again.\n• |cffffffffCooldown Manager, Growth From the Middle:|r a bar with fewer spells than its Columns now stays centred. A bar pinned by its side in Edit Mode moves a little.\n• |cffffffffAuras:|r square aura borders are thinner and use the action bars' bronze. Round aura rims use that colour too.\n• |cffffffffLoot Window:|r in Edit Mode, Blizzard's |cffffffffLoot Window|r checkbox now shows and hides FlareUI's. Its default spot moved to the right side of the screen (only if you never moved it).\n• |cffffffffMinimap, Shared Media borders:|r now as thick as on the chat and meters, and flush with the map's edge, its corners cut to fit. The Info Bar uses the same border.\n• |cffffffffRaid frames:|r |cffffffffSample Raid|r is now |cffffffffRaid Size|r.\n\n|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffRaid frames, Raid Size:|r Width, Height and Power Height for raids of up to 10, 25 or 40 players. Pick the size in Edit Mode, then set them. A size you never change keeps your current values.\n• |cffffffffIn a Battleground:|r a new choice in every Visibility list: action bars, unit frames, chat, meters, the Fake Cooldown Manager and Resource Bars.\n• |cffffffffFading|r for Party, Raid, Boss and Flag Carrier frames, as on the other unit frames.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• Party, Raid, Boss and Flag Carrier frames: a |cffffffffFading|r section in Edit Mode:\n      - |cffffffffVisibility|r, |cffffffffShow Speed|r, |cffffffffHide Speed|r, |cffffffffFaded Opacity|r, |cffffffffOpacity|r\n• Raid frames: |cffffffffRaid Size|r (Up to 10, 25 or 40 Players). Width, Height and Power Height are set per size. In a raid, the frames use the size that matches your group, and switch after a fight if it grows.\n\n|cffe6cc99Action Bars|r\n• Fake Cooldown Manager: |cffffffffShow Only When Ready|r (off). A spell on cooldown hides until it's ready. Its spot stays empty meanwhile.\n\n|cffe6cc99Chat|r\n• Edit Box: |cffffffffChat Style|r (IM Style or Classic Style), Blizzard's own setting. Takes effect at the next reload.\n• Each chat window keeps its own |cffffffffFont Size|r: right-click its tab.\n\n|cffe6cc99Buff Reminders|r\n• Mages: a |cffffffffMana Gem|r reminder. Click it to conjure the best gem you know.\n• Soulstone: |cffffffffKeep It On|r (right-click the icon) gets |cffffffffTanks|r.\n\n|cffe6cc99Minimap|r\n• Addon Buttons: |cffffffffOnly on Mouseover|r (off). The addon buttons on the minimap's edge hide until you point at the minimap or at one of them. Buttons in the drawer aren't affected.\n\n|cffe6cc99Loot|r\n• Loot Rolls: a |cffffffffClose|r button. It clears the rolls you answered or that ended. Rolls still waiting for your choice stay.\n• Loot Window: shows sample loot in Edit Mode, so you can see where it goes.\n\n|cffe6cc99Commands|r\n• |cffffd100/fui profile <name>|r switches to that profile, for a macro on a key or a radial. Type it alone to list your profiles.\n\n|cffe6cc99Translations|r\n• French, Simplified Chinese and Traditional Chinese updated for 7.1.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n• Swing bars: |cffffffffWaiting State|r, |cffffffffQueued Attack Colour|r and |cffffffffStand-Still Zone|r are switches again, on by default. If you turned one off before 7.1, it's off again.\n• Cast bars: a divider between the icon and the bar, in the bar's own border. On every cast bar with its icon and border on, nameplates included.\n• Loot Window: a bronze close button, further right, like the chat's and quest tracker's header buttons.\n• Loot Rolls: hold Shift anywhere on a roll's row to compare the item. Pressing Shift while pointing works too.\n• Unit frames: the Edit Mode box now covers the portrait and the level disc.\n• Border and bar texture lists never show Blizzard's own art. The Minimap's Border list included.\n• Nameplates: with Platynator or MFNameplates on, FlareUI's Nameplates step aside, as with Plater.\n• About and setup tour: the FlareUI Edit Mode layout code is updated.\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n• Damage Meter: Russian names showed as boxes in groups.\n• Chat: Russian names showed as boxes in the whisper line (\"Tell ...\").\n• Nameplates: combo points showed twice with another combo point addon, and on plates another addon had taken over.\n• Loot Feed: the settings preview now shows Round Icons.\n• Cooldown Manager: Growth From the Middle didn't stay centred with fewer spells.\n• Radial Menu: Sub-Radials on |cffffffffRemember|r forgot the last pick.\n• Loot Window: Blizzard's own loot box showed in Edit Mode next to FlareUI's.\n• Loot Rolls and Loot Feed drew over Blizzard's Edit Mode window.\n• Gryphons jumped around in Edit Mode with Action Bar 1 below 100% Icon Size.\n• Fonts: an error after some loading screens (\"calling 'GetFont' on bad self\").\n• Nameplates: a zoom setting could be put back on the wrong character." },
    { version = "7.1", text = "A big tidy-up of the settings: fewer rows, clearer names and a smarter Info Panel. Plus a batch of fixes from Discord.\n\n|cffffffffRestart the game fully after updating.|r This version adds a new file, and a /reload doesn't load it.\n\n|cffffffffWe need your help testing:|r\n• |cffffffffForever Style, rogues and druids:|r build combo points on a target. They should show round the target's portrait.\n• |cffffffffEdit Mode:|r open any unit frame. Check the new |cffffffffIcons|r, |cffffffffBar Effects|r and cast bar |cffffffffShow|r lists.\n• |cffffffffFriendly Name Only plates with Show Target's Plate:|r target a player, then clear the target. The name should show once, every time.\n• |cffffffffDruids with Keep Page 1 > On Shapeshift:|r go into Cat and Bear Form. Action Bar 1 should stay on its first page.\n\n|cffffd100Heads up|r\nSome things change even if you change nothing:\n• |cffffffffNameplates, Click-Through:|r now one setting for all plates. If you had it on for any plate type, it's now on for all of them.\n• |cffffffffNameplates, Name Only Mode:|r no longer greys out the other options. Show Plates in Combat and Show Target's Plate still give the plate its bar.\n• |cffffffffNameplates, Crowd Control and Defensives:|r their icons use the Auras look. Their own Aura Icon Shape, Aura Swipe and Aura Timer are gone.\n• |cffffffffForever Style:|r the name box always shows the full name, as on Blizzard's frames. Show Name is gone from Forever Style.\n• |cffffffffSwing bars:|r Waiting State, Queued Attack Colour and Stand-Still Zone are always on.\n• |cffffffffSwing bars, Off-Hand Swing:|r shows only with a weapon in your off hand.\n• |cffffffffQuest Tracker:|r finished quests always show \"(Complete)\".\n• |cffffffffBuff Reminders:|r the In Dungeons and In Raids timings are gone. Remind Before It Ends counts everywhere.\n• |cffffffffGryphons:|r now part of Quality of Life. They work with Action Bars off, and go back to Blizzard's with Quality of Life off.\n\n|cffffd100Highlights|r\n• |cffffffffInfo Panel:|r a small grey line under each option's title shows its default, whether it needs a reload, and what it needs to be on (in orange while that greys it out). Choice names in lists are gold, and every description was rewritten to be shorter and clearer.\n• |cffffffffEdit Mode, unit frames:|r related switches are now one dropdown each, on every frame:\n      - |cffffffffBar Effects:|r Bar Animations, Bar Edge Glow, Damage Trail\n      - |cffffffffIcons:|r resting, leader, PvP, ready check, raid markers and the rest, now in Look\n      - |cffffffffShow|r (cast bars): Icon, Spell Timer, Centred Spell Name, Edge Glow, Latency, Spell Pushback\n      - |cffffffffText|r (swing, flight, seal and duration bars): Name, Timer, Icon\n• |cffffffffCopy Look to All Frames:|r a button in each unit frame's Edit Mode window. It copies that frame's Bar Texture, Border, Absorb Texture, Background, Class Colours and Bar Effects to every other frame.\n\n|cffffd100New|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• Party: cast bar |cffffffffPosition|r (Above or Below). Auras on that side move past it.\n• Flag carriers: |cffffffffRange Check|r (off) and, in Modern Style, |cffffffffPortrait|r (None or Class Icon).\n• Main tank targets: |cffffffffTarget Border|r and |cffffffffShow Target Markers|r, as on party targets.\n• Pet: |cffffffffThreat Glow|r in every style, the simple pet frame too.\n\n|cffe6cc99Resource Bars|r\n• Health, power and mana bars: |cffffffffValues on Mouseover|r.\n• Druid Mana: |cffffffffIn Caster Form|r is now a choice in its |cffffffffVisibility|r list.\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• Name Only Mode: |cffffffffShow Level|r, the level in front of the name.\n\n|cffe6cc99Action Bars|r\n• |cffffffffKeep Page 1|r gets |cffffffffOn Shapeshift|r for druids' Cat and Bear Form (off).\n\n|cffe6cc99Minimap|r\n• |cffffffffBorder:|r your Shared Media borders, under a line below FlareUI Thick. They may not line up with the map's edge.\n• Round minimap: with |cffffffffBelow the Map|r on, the Info Bar can use all three cells.\n\n|cffffd100Changed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Settings, merged into one dropdown each|r\n• Action Bars: |cffffffffKeep Page 1|r (In Stealth, In Stances, On Shapeshift) and Fake Cooldown Manager |cffffffffBars|r.\n• Nameplates: |cffffffffTarget Highlight|r, |cffffffffThreat Effects|r, |cffffffffQuest Marks|r (Icon, Progress), |cffffffffKick Ready|r (Colour, Mark), |cffffffffGroup Colours|r (Party, Raid) and |cffffffffUnder the Name|r (Title, Guild).\n• Meters: |cffffffffPull Warning|r (Flash, Sound; the sound can play on its own now) and |cffffffffAuto Reset|r.\n• Chat: |cffffffffNames|r (Better Player Names, Better NPC Names, Level Before Names).\n• Tooltips: |cffffffffGuild|r (Off, Name, Name and Rank).\n• General: |cffffffffLanguage|r, with Game Language first.\n• Bags & Looting: |cffffffffLoot Window|r (Off, Grow Down, Grow Up). Elixirs: |cffffffffAll in Your Bags|r is now the top choice of |cffffffffElixirs and More|r.\n• Quality of Life: |cffffffffRumble|r (Alerts, Procs). Buff Reminders: |cffffffffHide|r (In Rested Areas, While Mounted) in Edit Mode.\n\n|cffe6cc99Settings, moved and renamed|r\n• Quality of Life: Extras and Systems are one |cffffffffExtras|r tab. General: the General tab is now |cffffffffAccount|r, and fonts are split into |cffffffffGlobal Font|r and |cffffffffGame Fonts|r.\n• |cffffffffFake CM|r is now |cffffffffFake Cooldown Manager|r everywhere. Its note says why you'd use it over Blizzard's.\n• Sizes in % are now |cffffffffScale|r (Combat Text, Drawer Button, Name Only, Level Disc).\n• Nameplate Font is now |cffffffffWorld Names Font|r: it sets the names over characters in the world and on Blizzard's nameplates.\n• Nameplates: Health Text is |cffffffffBar Text|r, Threat Percentage is |cffffffffThreat Text|r. Show Plates in Combat moved to Visibility.\n• Tooltips: Coloured Borders and Class-Coloured Names moved to the first tab.\n• Raid: the group order row is now |cffffffffGroup Order|r, and Groups is |cffffffffOrientation|r.\n• Many smaller regroups, so every section reads in the same order.\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• |cffffffffBar Text|r on mirrored frames: Left and Right in the menu are now the screen's sides. Your frames look the same as before.\n• Edit Mode: |cffffffffCombo Points|r moved to Look. Opacity on Buff Reminders moved to Fading.\n\n|cffe6cc99Removed|r\n• Pet: |cffffffffOnly My Debuffs|r (it only emptied the list).\n• Target and target of target: |cffffffffHas a Target|r in Visibility (always true on those frames).\n\n|cffffd100Fixed|r\n\n|cffe6cc99Unit Frames|r\n• Forever Style: combo points didn't show on the target frame.\n• The player frame's |cffffffffCast Name|r and |cffffffffSpell Timer|r fonts showed while the Player Cast Bar was on, though they don't style it. They now hide then; the bar's fonts are under |cffffffffPlayer Cast Bar|r.\n\n|cffe6cc99Nameplates|r\n• Friendly Name Only plates with |cffffffffShow Target's Plate|r and |cffffffffNames Above Plate|r: the name went missing on your target and showed twice after.\n\n|cffe6cc99Minimap|r\n• The |cffffffffFlareUI Minimap Button|r switch was greyed out with Drawer Style Off.\n\n|cffe6cc99Edit Mode|r\n• Raid: two rows were called Sort By.\n• Loot Rolls: |cffffffffFaded Opacity|r showed above the switch that turns it on." },
}
